1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,816
Mia's Halloween costume. One hundred eighty dollars. Worn once.

2
00:00:03,866 --> 00:00:05,792
Plus decorations. Plus candy.

3
00:00:05,692 --> 00:00:07,996
Plus a second outfit for the party.

4
00:00:08,046 --> 00:00:10,356
This year's average Halloween budget?

5
00:00:10,256 --> 00:00:12,387
About one hundred fifteen dollars.

6
00:00:12,437 --> 00:00:14,550
You? Costume from your own closet.

7
00:00:14,450 --> 00:00:16,208
Twelve dollars for one prop.

8
00:00:16,258 --> 00:00:18,792
Candy? One big bag on the list. That's it.

9
00:00:18,842 --> 00:00:21,410
Then November first, you go back to the store.

10
00:00:21,460 --> 00:00:24,447
Next year's decorations. Often half off or more.

11
00:00:24,497 --> 00:00:26,925
Follow for one simple money move every

12
00:00:26,825 --> 00:00:28,334
day. Because next year,

13
00:00:28,234 --> 00:00:29,927
Mia pays full price again.
